==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]].
*1 [[Mr. Mole]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Henry]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Dolphina]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Croakley]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Assassin Bear]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Assassin Bear]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Assassin Bear]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Croakley, Henry and Mr. Mole tag team to slow, freeze and knockback your cats, then Li'l Bun Buns and Dolphinas chip your cats' health, while Assassin Bears appear to end you if you fire the [[Cat Cannon]] too early. Doge Base will destroy everything if you push too far.

Fast units, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]] are very effective here, as they don't require a lot of timing to get into Croakley's and Henry's blind spots. Conversely, long-ranged cats won't do much, as they'll end either frozen and slowed by Croakley and Henry, or sniped by Mr. Mole and Dolphina. [[:Category:Cats with Slow Immunity|Units that are immune to Slow]] or [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Freeze]] can be useful here, but you must be sure they don't get affected by the debuff they aren't immune to.

For {{4c}}, use [[Talents|talented]] Awakened Bahamut Cat and rushers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to obliterate the first few enemies. Afterwards, use [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] to infiltrate Croakley and Henry's blind spots and block the Doge Base's Wave Attacks.

